---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/Briefing.css';
---

<Layout title="ORION // OP 6: Rearguard - Briefing" description="Field briefing for Operation Rearguard - a fighting withdrawal through Zone-21 to pull Maj. Gen. Antti Virtanen out before the base falls." nav={[{ href: '/orion-fimbulwinter/mission-control/', label: '<- MISSION CONTROL' }, { href: '#situation', label: 'SITUATION' }, { href: '#mission', label: 'MISSION' }, { href: '#ground', label: 'GROUND' }, { href: '#execution', label: 'EXECUTION' }, { href: '#roe', label: 'ROE' }, { href: '#support', label: 'SUPPORT' }]} footer="ORION INTERNATIONAL - ZONE-21 // FIMBULWINTER - OP 6: REARGUARD - BRIEFING" decryptLines={['ORION SECURE UPLINK - CHANNEL 21', 'AUTHENTICATING OPERATOR...', 'CLEARANCE CONFIRMED - FIELD COMMAND', 'DECRYPTING DOSSIER: OPERATION REARGUARD']}>
  <div class="briefing-actions"><button class="print-opord" type="button">PRINT OPORD</button></div>
  <section id="situation" class="briefing-section"><h1 class="op-name">SITUATION</h1><h2 class="op-title">OPERATION REARGUARD</h2><div class="reveal"><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Zone-21 is falling. Colonel-General Igor Chernov never lost the initiative on this line and is driving on the FDF command post unopposed. The outer ring is breaking. This is not a holding action anymore — it's a fighting withdrawal, and command needs three things out before the base goes: intelligence, people, and time.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Before comms went dark, Orion intelligence flagged a server in the nearby town holding sensitive material — targeting data, codebook entries — that cannot be left for the 44th to recover intact.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Maj. Gen. Antti Virtanen, commander of the FDF South Karelia Brigade and Odin's official counterpart, is trapped in the collapsing CP bunker. He's the last direct line to Finnish air support coordination in this sector. If the post comes down on top of him, that coordination goes with it — and so does any chance of putting Finnish air back in this fight.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">An AC-130J is on station with a limited window of time and munitions. A Su-35 is active and contesting the airspace. Valkyrie is airborne in a Chinook, tasked to extract at LZ Kotka once the general is clear.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">This isn't a mission that ends in Zone-21 held. It ends when the team, the intelligence, and the general are out, and everything behind them is Chernov's problem, not command's.</p></div></section>
  <section id="mission" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">MISSION</h2><h3 class="op-title">TASKING</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">FIELD COMMAND DIRECTIVE</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Orion elements will form a column, pull the sensitive material from the town server, clear the Russian observers watching the route, extract Maj. Gen. Virtanen alive and conscious from the CP bunker, and rendezvous with Valkyrie at LZ Kotka for extraction.</p></div></section>
  <section id="ground"><h2 class="op-name">GROUND</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD NAVIGATION</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">TERRAIN // ZONE-21, SECTOR UNSPECIFIED</div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">A town server holding the flagged material (Phase 1), reachable but not for long. A ring of Russian observers covering the route beyond it (Phase 2). The CP bunker at the core of the base, the most heavily contested point on the map (Phase 3). LZ Kotka, Valkyrie's assigned pickup point, some distance clear of the fighting (Phase 4). There is no fixed route between any of these — the ring is collapsing as the operation runs, and the column will have to reroute as it goes.</p><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim);font-size:12px;">Exact positions are released to ground command once Eden placement is locked. Positions are directional, not gridded.</p></div></section>
  <section id="execution" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">EXECUTION</h2><h3 class="op-title">ORDER OF BATTLE</h3><div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-1" data-phase="1"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="1" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 1 / 4</div><h3>Extract the Archive</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Connect to the server in town and pull the data. The transfer takes real time and cannot be rushed — hold the site for the duration. A relay dish nearby needs to stay powered and intact for the transfer to run at full speed; lose it and the exposure window gets longer, not shorter.</p></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-2" data-phase="2"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="2" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 2 / 4</div><h3>Silence the Spotters</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Several Russian forward observers cover the next stretch of the route. They go down together. One taken out early buys the rest time to call in artillery on the column before the position is fully silenced — coordinate before anyone opens up.</p></div><div class="phase reveal" id="execution-phase-3" data-phase="3"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="3" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 3 / 4</div><h3>Extract the General</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The column reaches the CP sector, the most heavily defended stop on the map. Free Virtanen from the wreckage. His condition on contact depends on how much damage the CP took before the team arrives — walking, carried, or litter. He needs to stay conscious: he's the only one who can confirm the last air coordination traffic.</p></div><div class="phase climax reveal" id="execution-phase-4" data-phase="4"><label class="phase-check"><input type="checkbox" data-checklist-phase="4" /><span>PHASE COMPLETE</span></label><div class="num">PHASE 4 / 4</div><h3>Extraction</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Move to LZ Kotka with Virtanen and link up with Valkyrie. AC-130J covers the pickup while its window lasts. The Su-35 has been a problem all operation — expect it to make its move here, not before.</p></div><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll" style="color:var(--dim); font-size:12px;">Ground commanders retain discretionary authority over internal task allocation and approach across all phases.</p></div></section>
  <section id="roe" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">RULES OF ENGAGEMENT</h2><h3 class="op-title">FIELD RESTRICTIONS</h3><div class="intel reveal"><div class="head">ROE // EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY</div><ul class="reveal decrypt-scroll"><li>Any Russian element, garrison, or patrol observed, in contact, or confirmed at a designated objective is hostile.</li><li>Getting Virtanen out alive and conscious takes priority over holding any ground, including the CP itself once he's clear.</li><li>Phase 2 observers go down as close to simultaneously as possible. Coordinate before engaging — early contact costs the whole column later.</li><li>Lethal force is authorised against confirmed hostile positions without further clearance.</li><li>Self-defence is authorised at all times without prior command approval.</li><li>No obligation to hold or retake lost sections of the perimeter. This operation ends at extraction, not at the line.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section id="support" class="briefing-section"><h2 class="op-name">SUPPORT</h2><h3 class="op-title">AVAILABLE ASSETS</h3><div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">AIR SUPPORT</div><h3>Valkyrie</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Airborne in a Chinook, tasked to LZ Kotka for the Phase 4 pickup. AC-130J is on station with a limited time/munitions window for Phases 2-4 — do not plan the extraction around it remaining available the whole operation. A Su-35 is active in the sector and can force it, or Valkyrie, off station or out of position. FA-18 support is not guaranteed.</p></div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">COMMS</div><h3>Virtanen Only</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">Virtanen is the only source for the last confirmed air coordination traffic once extracted. Treat all other incoming sector traffic as unconfirmed until corroborated.</p></div><div class="phase reveal"><div class="num">GROUND</div><h3>Whatever's Running</h3><p class="reveal decrypt-scroll">The column forms at the start of Phase 1 from whatever vehicles are still running — not a clean, pre-assigned convoy. Damage taken carries through the rest of the operation. The base is not held after this operation; Zone-21 is lost regardless of outcome.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="operator-note" class="operator-note reveal" aria-label="Operator's note"><div class="head">OFF-RECORD // FOR THE PERSON WHO READS TO THE END</div><p>This isn't a mission you win. Zone-21 is gone the moment this briefing gets read — nothing in these four phases changes that.</p><p>What changes is whether Chernov gets the archive, whether the observers who saw you coming get to say so, and whether Virtanen is still breathing when Valkyrie sets down. Those are the things that carry past tonight. The base isn't one of them.</p><p>Get him out conscious. He's the only reason anyone still has a phone number for Finnish air support tomorrow.</p></section>
  <script>
    const unlockPhase = (phase: string) => {
      const blip = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(`.blip[data-phase="${phase}"]`);
      if (!blip) return;
      blip.classList.remove('locked');
      blip.removeAttribute('aria-hidden');
      blip.removeAttribute('tabindex');
    };
    document.querySelectorAll('.blip').forEach((blip) => blip.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const target = document.querySelector(blip.dataset.target || '');
      if (!(target instanceof HTMLElement) || blip.classList.contains('locked')) return;
      const reducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      target.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reducedMotion ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      target.classList.remove('flash');
      void target.offsetWidth;
      target.classList.add('flash');
      window.setTimeout(() => target.classList.remove('flash'), 1500);
    }));
    const phaseObserver = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (!entry.isIntersecting || !(entry.target instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
        const phase = entry.target.dataset.phase;
        if (!phase) return;
        unlockPhase(phase);
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.45 });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.phase[data-phase]').forEach((phase) => phaseObserver.observe(phase));

    const checklistKey = 'orion-checklist-op6';
    const completePhases = new Set<number>(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(checklistKey) || '[]'));
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-checklist-phase]').forEach((input) => {
      const phase = Number(input.dataset.checklistPhase);
      input.checked = completePhases.has(phase);
      input.addEventListener('change', () => {
        input.checked ? completePhases.add(phase) : completePhases.delete(phase);
        localStorage.setItem(checklistKey, JSON.stringify([...completePhases]));
      });
    });

    document.querySelector('.print-opord')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
  </script>
</Layout>
